# Broadcast media: digital TV (DVB), analog TV, FM radio, SDR, and the media
# test drivers. Neither product has a tuner and neither is a machine anyone
# plugs a TV stick into; this was building 163 DVB frontend and tuner modules.
#
# MEDIA_SUPPORT_FILTER is what makes the per-type switches selectable at all --
# with it off Kconfig forces every MEDIA_*_SUPPORT to y, which is how these got
# enabled in the first place.
#
# Deliberately kept, and safe as cheap SoCs are added later:
#   CAMERA   -- the laptop's UVC webcam, and any USB camera
#   PLATFORM -- SoC video codecs and ISPs, which is exactly what Rockchip,
#               MediaTek and Amlogic boards need. Unrelated to broadcast.
CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT_FILTER=y
CONFIG_MEDIA_CAMERA_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MEDIA_PLATFORM_SUPPORT=y
# CONFIG_MEDIA_ANALOG_TV_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_DIGITAL_TV_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_RADIO_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SDR_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_TEST_SUPPORT is not set
